team_request.body:
Hello,

{{requester}} asks to create the team "{{team}}".

Message: {{message}}

Approve or reject the request in the administration area:

    {{url}}

team_approved.body:
Hello,

Your team "{{team}}" has been approved. You can now invite its members and set up its access to the TAK server:

    {{url}}

team_rejected.body:
Hello,

Your request to create the team "{{team}}" was not approved.

Reason given: {{note}}

event_invitation.body:
Hello,

The team "{{host}}" invites your team "{{team}}" to the event "{{event}}".

    Start: {{start}}
    End:   {{end}}

If you accept, the members of your team and those of the other participating teams see each other on the TAK server for the duration of the event, through a channel named {{channel}} that appears by itself in ATAK and iTAK and disappears at the end. Nothing has to be installed or set up on the devices.

As a team leader, accept or decline on your team's page (the dates are shown there in your own time zone):

    {{url}}

event_left.body:
Hello,

The team "{{team}}" no longer takes part in your event "{{event}}". Its members stopped seeing the other teams, and being seen by them, at once.

    {{url}}

event_rescheduled.body:
Hello,

The team "{{host}}" changed the dates of the event "{{event}}". It now runs:

    Start: {{start}}
    End:   {{end}}

The channel {{channel}} appears and disappears by itself at these times. Your team's page shows them in your own time zone:

    {{url}}

alert_digest.body:
Hello,

{{sections}}

The monitoring page has the details and the history:

    {{url}}

You receive this message because you are an administrator of this platform. An alert is announced once, recalled at most once a day while it lasts, and announced again when it is over.
